# mm.touch.cst816

The Goodtek CST816 capacitive touch controller, over portable mm.mcu I2C and
GPIO. It contains no vendor header and no board pin number: a board's provider
supplies the wiring and this module drives the protocol.

The register map is eight-bit, and the one point the controller holds is four
bytes: the high nibbles of the two coordinates, then the low bytes. The
finger-count register says how many contacts are on the panel; this driver
decodes the one the reference driver reports and treats the rest as not
available, because a coordinate that is not decoded is not reported.

Modelled on Waveshare's reference driver for the RP2350-Touch-LCD-1.54. Three
things in that driver are deliberately not reproduced. Its interrupt handler is
absent, because mm.touch is polled and mm.mcu has no callback registration.
Its gesture mode is absent, because gestures are events and mm.touch reports
points; the controller is left in point mode. Its mirror transform is absent,
because mm.touch reports the panel's own coordinates and mapping belongs to
whoever knows how the panel is mounted.
